.TH RGBDNS 7 "2026-07-30" "rgbdns 0.3.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
rgbdns \- authoritative DNS, AXFR, recursion, and djbdns-compatible tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rgbdns-setup primary
--data FILE [OPTIONS]
.br
.B rgbdns-setup secondary
--zone NAME [--zone NAME ...] --primary ADDRESS[:PORT] [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Debian package installs the rgbdns program family and hardened systemd
units. It does not start a DNS service until an administrator supplies a zone
data file or configures a secondary.
.PP
The authoritative server reads
.IR /var/lib/rgbdns/tinydns/data.cdb .
The human-editable source is
.IR /var/lib/rgbdns/tinydns/data .
The setup command compiles the source atomically before starting the service.
.PP
A fresh package installation does not infer or activate a role. Run
.B rgbdns-setup
once to configure a primary or secondary. Package upgrades restore the picker
and timer units belonging to the role already recorded under
.IR /etc/rgbdns .
Run the opposite setup role to repurpose a host; it removes the prior role
configuration and disables its automation before enabling the new role.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/rgbdns/tinydns.env
Authoritative listen address, port, compiled data path, and optional AXFR
client CIDR allow-list.
.TP
.I /etc/rgbdns/secondary.env
Secondary primary-server endpoint.
.TP
.I /etc/rgbdns/zones
Canonical one-zone-per-line secondary zone list.
.TP
.I /etc/rgbdns/zones-drop.env
Configured scp drop path and required upload owner.
.TP
.I /etc/rgbdns/data-drop.env
Configured primary-data scp drop path and required upload owner.
.TP
.I /var/lib/rgbdns/tinydns/data
Tinydns-format zone source.
.SH SERVICES
.BR rgbdns-tinydns.service ,
.BR rgbdns-secondary-sync.service ,
.BR rgbdns-secondary-sync.timer ,
.BR rgbdns-zones-import.service ,
.BR rgbdns-data-import.service ,
.BR rgbdns-data.path ,
and
.BR rgbdns-zones.path .
.SH DOCUMENTATION
See
.I /usr/share/doc/rgbdns/debian.md.gz
for complete primary, secondary, firewall, testing, and troubleshooting
instructions.
